{%- doc -%}
  Outputs the handle of the collection a product breadcrumb should show: the collection in the URL
  when the product was opened from one, otherwise its most specific collection (fewest products),
  so catch-all collections such as "All products" lose to "Knit Polo". Ties keep Shopify's order.
  Shared by the visible breadcrumb (main-product) and its BreadcrumbList (structured-data).

  @param {object} product - The product

  @example
  {%- capture handle -%}{% render 'breadcrumb-collection', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  if collection != blank and collection.handle != 'all'
    echo collection.handle
  else
    assign best = blank
    for candidate in product.collections
      if candidate.handle == 'all' or candidate.handle == 'frontpage'
        continue
      endif
      if best == blank or candidate.all_products_count < best.all_products_count
        assign best = candidate
      endif
    endfor
    echo best.handle
  endif
-%}
